*** Add File:README-multilang-integration.md
+Multi-language integration skeletons (Go, Node, Java)
+
+What is included
+- Go: cosign-verifier minimal service + Dockerfile + k8s manifests
+- Node: TypeScript admission-like webhook + simple admin UI (static) + Dockerfiles
+- Java: minimal Spring Boot app and pom demonstrating OTEL agent usage
+
+How to use (quick)
+- Build Go image:
+  cd go/cosign-verifier && docker build -t your-registry/cosign-verifier:latest .
+- Deploy in cluster and configure webhook CA bundle; replace placeholders in k8s/webhook-configuration.yaml.
+
+- Start Node webhook (dev):
+  cd node/webhook && npm ci && npm run dev
+
+- Admin UI quick:
+  cd node/admin-ui && npm ci && node server.js
+
+- Java OTEL:
+  cd java/otel-springboot && mvn package
+  Run with the OpenTelemetry Java agent as described in java/otel-springboot/README.md
+
+Security & production notes
+- Do not use PoC cosign execution patterns in production — integrate with Key Management (KMS) and cosign libraries, validate policies and signatures using verified keys.
+- Webhooks must be served over TLS with a proper CA bundle; use cert-manager to provision webhook certificates and populate caBundle in ValidatingWebhookConfiguration.
+- Harden service accounts and RBAC for verifier and webhook components.
+
